          }
        },
        "heading_7KXKRf": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Our philosophy",
            "heading_size": "h1"
          }
        },
        "text_jMaqpG": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>We built Settle because ADHD care in the UK is broken in a specific, fixable way.</p><p><br/>The NHS waitlist for adult ADHD assessment now sits at five to seven years in most regions. GPs are not trained or supported to refer in any consistent way. Many private providers prescribe and then disappear, leaving patients without follow-up care or annual reviews. And every step of the process - diagnosis, titration, ongoing care, repeat prescriptions - happens at a different place, with a different person, often with weeks of waiting between each.</p><p><br/>Settle's model is the opposite. One clinician sees you from assessment to annual review. One pharmacy dispenses your medication. One brand is accountable for the whole experience. We've structured the business so the parts that usually fall apart - the handoffs, the gaps between providers, the lost prescriptions - can't happen, because there are no handoffs to fail.</p><p><br/>We won't be right for every patient. If you want a quick, low-touch service that runs entirely on automation, there are cheaper providers. If what you want is to be properly diagnosed, properly medicated, and properly looked after - by the same psychiatrist, for as long as you need them - that's what we built.</p>",
            "text_style": "body",
            "text_size": "medium"
          }
        }
      },
